From Ethiopia to Kenya, a flurry of local manufacturers and craftsmen have partnered with Western apparel brands to make stylish shoes produced and sourced entirely on the African continent. There are rubber-soled cotton canvas low-tops from Mombasa, suede tennis shoes from Addis Ababa and crepe-soled nubuck loafers that incorporate materials from Mauritius, Liberia and South Africa.
